# MiliUI Usage Terms

Copyright (c) 2026 MyPingO. All rights reserved.

MiliUI is **not open source**. It is provided for Miliastra creators to use in
their own projects while keeping MiliUI itself as one maintained project.

## You may

- use official MiliUI releases in your own Miliastra projects;
- publish and monetize Miliastra projects that use MiliUI;
- write and modify your own game/UI code that uses MiliUI;
- copy and adapt the public example files for projects that use MiliUI;
- share links to the official MiliUI repository and official releases;
- report bugs, suggest features, and contribute documentation/examples.

## Please do not

- fork MiliUI and publish it as your own framework;
- redistribute, mirror, or re-upload MiliUI itself as a separate download;
- publish modified, repackaged, or renamed versions of MiliUI;
- bundle MiliUI into another UI framework/toolkit for redistribution;
- sell or sublicense MiliUI itself;
- remove or misrepresent MiliUI authorship/ownership;
- use the MiliUI name or branding to make an unofficial build look official;
- publish or redistribute private MiliUI development source if you obtain access
  to it.

Using the official MiliUI runtime inside your own Miliastra project is allowed
and is not considered prohibited redistribution.

## Your own work remains yours

Your game code, UI code, assets, and other original work built around MiliUI
remain your own. These terms only apply to MiliUI itself and the files distributed
as part of MiliUI.

## Contributions and feedback

If you send documentation, examples, fixes, or other material specifically for
possible inclusion in MiliUI, you allow the MiliUI project to use, edit, and
include that contribution.

## Beta software

MiliUI may change during beta, including API changes. No guarantee is made that
every beta release will remain compatible with earlier versions.

MiliUI is provided as-is, without a warranty.

If you are unsure whether something you want to do is allowed, ask before
redistributing MiliUI itself.
